# OCI 11.2's password change for pyo_pwchg (#2463), without the TTI_80SES
# piggyback ahead of it: an AUTH of mode 0x102, an empty AUTH_SESSKEY (flag 1),
# the current and the new password encrypted (64 hex digits each), the session's
# own pairs and its ALTER SESSION.
# Captured 2026-11-07 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8;
# OCIPasswordChange on an open session, called through ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE
# 11.2.0.2, a DEDICATED session, for a throwaway account dropped after. The TTC
# payload, without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset
# column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
